{"case_id":"C069","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":99,"change_types":["bug_fix","test_addition","integer_shift_type_correction"],"affected_functions":["decodeVByte","meshopt_decodeIndexBuffer"],"reason":"The production change only makes the existing variable-byte decoding shift explicitly unsigned, and the added regression test supplies a malformed byte stream to the already-existing meshopt_decodeIndexBuffer API. The harness already invokes meshopt_decodeIndexBuffer with arbitrary fuzzer-controlled data, the same count of 66 used by the new test, and both supported index strides. No entry point, protocol, initialization, configuration, state requirement, or input constraint changed, so harness maintenance is not needed.","evidence":["In src/indexcodec.cpp, `result |= (group & 127) << shift;` changes only to `result |= unsigned(group & 127) << shift;` inside `decodeVByte`.","The new `decodeIndexMalformedVByte` regression test calls `meshopt_decodeIndexBuffer(decoded, 66, input, sizeof(input))` and expects rejection.","The existing harness calls `fuzzDecoder(data, size, 2, meshopt_decodeIndexBuffer)` and `fuzzDecoder(data, size, 4, meshopt_decodeIndexBuffer)` using arbitrary input bytes.","`fuzzDecoder` fixes `count = 66`, matching the regression test's decoded element count, while passing fuzzer-controlled `data` and `size` to the decoder."],"recommended_action":"Keep the existing fuzz harness unchanged."}
